guide forever/class/priest/desperate-prayer-and-chastise
title Desperate Prayer and Chastise
category Class
class Priest
folder Priest
faction Alliance
race Human,Dwarf
levels 10-20
zone Ironforge
keywords Desperate Prayer, Chastise, A Lack of Fear, High Priest Rohan, High Priestess Laurena, Hall of Mysteries, Mystic Ward, Dwarf, Human, racial, Priest
reward spell 13908 "Desperate Prayer"
reward spell 1277331 "Chastise (Dwarves)"
why The Human and Dwarf priest spells: Desperate Prayer at 10, Chastise for Dwarves at 20.

# The Desperate Prayer quest at 10 (5639, Humans and Dwarves) and the Dwarf
# Priest Chastise quest at 20 (5641), both from High Priest Rohan in
# Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries.
# Sources: quests.json and npcs.json for the givers; Forever's
# Priest class quest list (data/local/quest-audit/):
# Chastise (5641, 5645, 5647, updated) is "Renamed from A Lack of Fear",
# "Rewards: adds Chastise", "no longer Fear Ward"; the Desperate Prayer
# quests (5634-5640, updated) have reworded or removed objective text, and
# 5634 "no longer Starts at High Priestess Laurena".
# Races: Forever's quest data (quests 5634-5640, checked
# 2026-10-14) lists 5635, 5637 and 5639 for Humans and Dwarves, the others
# for Dwarves; this guide follows that. Third-party Forever sites
# (classicwowforever.com/racials) say Humans no longer learn Desperate
# Prayer; the quest data does not confirm it, so the step stays open to
# Humans: skip it if Rohan offers you nothing.
# Who takes it: Forever's quest data still names High Priestess
# Laurena in Stormwind as the ender of every Desperate Prayer quest, while
# the reworded Forever text says "Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge".
# The turn-in follows the ender data (Laurena); the tip says to ask Rohan
# first.
# alliance/dwarf-gnome/01-dun-morogh carries Desperate Prayer on the route
# (5637, from Maxan Anvol in Kharanos) and alliance/04-redridge-mountains
# and 06-ashenvale carry Chastise (5645, from High Priestess Laurena); this
# guide repeats them for anyone off the route. The game offers one quest of
# each set (the others are breadcrumbs from priest trainers in other
# cities). Not checked in game: written from the sources above.

step Desperate Prayer
  tip At 10, go to High Priest Rohan in the Hall of Mysteries, in Ironforge's Mystic Ward. Forever's quest text names Rohan, but the quest data has High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light take it: try Rohan first, then Laurena (the Deeprun Tram links the cities).
  level 10
  accept 5639                                 -- High Priest Rohan

step High Priestess Laurena
  zone Stormwind City
  tip If Rohan did not take it: High Priestess Laurena is in the Cathedral of Light. Take the Deeprun Tram from Tinker Town.
  turnin 5639                                 -- Desperate Prayer

step Chastise
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  tip At 20, High Priest Rohan teaches Chastise. High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind and Priestess Alathea in Darnassus send you to him with a quest of the same name.
  level 20
  accept 5641                                 -- High Priest Rohan
  turnin 5641                                 -- High Priest Rohan: Chastise
